      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To better understand and protect yourself, it's essential to review your account terms and conditions, as well as any disclosed \"roi\" or usage limits that may be tied to your account. Look for any clauses that could be used to penalty-ride you, and carefully consider whether these limits are reasonable given your account history. Additionally, review your account settings and notify your credit union's customer service if any changes are being made to your account without your approval. You may also want to consider escalating the issue to a supervisor or reporting it to the Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB).",
